      content: `If you manage a commercial building, hospital, educational facility, aged care home, retail centre or government property in Sydney, there is a high probability the building has a [Dynalite](https://www.signify.com/en-au/brands/dynalite), [C-Bus](https://www.se.com/au/en/work/products/product-launch/cbus/), RAPIX or DALI lighting control system. There is also a high probability it has not been properly serviced since it was commissioned.

George works with facility managers across Greater Sydney to provide specialist lighting control maintenance, compliance support and fault response for buildings that the original installer may no longer service.

**Why Lighting Control Systems Need Specialist Maintenance**

Dynalite, C-Bus and RAPIX systems are not like standard electrical infrastructure. They have network topologies, software configurations, and integration points that drift over time \u2014 especially in buildings where electrical, HVAC, BMS or AV work is done periodically by third-party contractors. Every time an electrician does work near a lighting control switchboard without the right knowledge, there is a risk of programming corruption, address conflicts, or integration failures.

**The Four Things Facility Managers Should Know**

First, know what system you have. Is it Dynalite, C-Bus, RAPIX, or a combination? Each platform requires different tools and accreditation to service properly. Second, know whether a current programming backup exists. A single hardware failure or power event without a backup could wipe all programmed scenes. Third, understand your emergency lighting compliance obligations under [NCC 2022](https://ncc.abcb.gov.au/) DALI-2 requirements. Fourth, have a specialist on call before a fault occurs \u2014 not after.

**Planned Maintenance for Commercial and Institutional Buildings**

George offers planned maintenance agreements for commercial buildings, strata complexes and institutional facilities across Greater Sydney. This includes scheduled system health checks, programming backups, scene and schedule updates as building use changes, DALI emergency lighting testing and documentation, and priority fault response.

For lighting control maintenance, compliance support or fault response across Sydney CBD, North Shore, Eastern Suburbs, Parramatta, Sutherland Shire or anywhere in Greater Sydney, contact Sydney Automation Co. on 0422 469 739 or service@sydneyautomationco.com.au.

**Long-Tail Keywords for Facility Managers**

Searches: “facility manager lighting control Sydney”, “commercial building C-Bus maintenance”, “Dynalite planned maintenance Sydney”, “DALI emergency lighting facility management”, “[NABERS](https://www.nabers.gov.au/) energy efficiency lighting control”.

See also our [Strata Managers: Who to Call When Your Building](/blog/strata-managers-lighting-control-sydney) and [DALI-2 Compliance for NSW Commercial Buildings](/blog/dali2-compliance-nsw-commercial) for related information.

**Service Agreements for Sydney Facilities**

Sydney Automation Co. offers service agreements for commercial buildings and managed facilities across Greater Sydney. A typical agreement covers: one annual system health check and programming backup; priority response for urgent faults (same or next business day); quarterly DALI emergency lighting test and report for [NCC 2022](https://ncc.abcb.gov.au/) compliance; and scene and schedule updates as building use changes.

Service agreements are available for buildings running [C-Bus](https://www.se.com/au/en/work/products/product-launch/cbus/), [Dynalite](https://www.signify.com/en-au/brands/dynalite), [RAPIX](https://ozuno.com/rapix-lighting-control-system/) or DALI-only systems. Call 0422 469 739 or visit our [Strata & FM page](/strata) for full details on service agreements for managed buildings. Email service@sydneyautomationco.com.au to discuss your building’s requirements.`
